            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$2x^2+3x-6=2(x+1)^2-(x+1)-7$.\n\nWrite $x=(x+1)-1$ and expand the outer brackets.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2x^2+3x-6&=2\\big((x+1)^2-2(x+1)+1\\big)+3\\big((x+1)-1\\big)-6\\\\2x^2+3x-6&=2(x+1)^2+(-4+3)(x+1)+(2-3-6)\\\\2x^2+3x-6&=2(x+1)^2-(x+1)-7.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 40
